  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:deployed-regret-certificate",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "On the simultaneous event \\(p\\in\\mathcal C_n(\\alpha)\\), every data-dependent deployed mixture \\(\\widetilde q_x\\in\\Delta_K\\) satisfies \\(R_x(\\widetilde q_x,p_x)\\leq\\overline R_{x,n}(\\widetilde q_x;\\alpha)\\) for every \\(x\\). Consequently, with probability at least \\(1-\\alpha\\), all deployed-stratum inequalities hold simultaneously, including the reported numerical primal--dual gap.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "p",
      "p_x",
      "\\mathcal C_n(\\alpha)",
      "n",
      "\\alpha",
      "\\widetilde q_x",
      "\\Delta_K",
      "R_x(q,p_x)",
      "\\overline R_{x,n}(\\widetilde q_x;\\alpha)",
      "\\mathcal X"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:iid-sampling",
      "def:cp-fiber",
      "def:deployed-certificate",
      "lem:joint-saddle-background",
      "lem:clopper-pearson-cell-coverage",
      "thm:cp-correspondence-coverage"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix a realization on which \\(p\\in\\mathcal C_n(\\alpha)\\), a stratum \\(x\\), and any measurable or nonmeasurable-in-the-data realized choice \\(\\widetilde q_x\\in\\Delta_K\\).  The true table is one of the points over which the defining supremum is taken, and hence\n\\[\n R_x(\\widetilde q_x,p_x)\n =\\max_{b\\in\\mathcal A}h_{\\mathcal M_x(p_x)}(e_b-\\widetilde q_x)\n \\leq\\sup_{p'\\in\\mathcal C_n(\\alpha)}\\max_{b\\in\\mathcal A}h_{\\mathcal M_x(p'_x)}(e_b-\\widetilde q_x)\n =\\overline R_{x,n}(\\widetilde q_x;\\alpha).\n\\]\nThis pointwise argument allows arbitrary data dependence of the deployed rule.  If a numerical primal--dual pair reports an upper endpoint \\(U\\) and a verified nonnegative gap \\(\\gamma\\), weak duality gives that the exact supremum is at most \\(U+\\gamma\\); the augmentation required in \\texttt{def:deployed-certificate} therefore preserves the displayed inequality.\n\nFor the probability claim, \\(\\mathrm{lem{:}clopper\\text{-}pearson\\text{-}cell\\text{-}coverage}\\) gives conditional coverage of each of the \\(2K|\\mathcal X||\\mathcal Z|\\) cells at error \\(\\alpha/(2K|\\mathcal X||\\mathcal Z|)\\).  The conditional union bound used in \\(\\mathrm{thm{:}cp\\text{-}correspondence\\text{-}coverage}\\) therefore gives the simultaneous event of probability at least \\(1-\\alpha\\), on which the compatible true table belongs to \\(\\mathcal C_n(\\alpha)\\).  The displayed deterministic inequality then holds for every stratum simultaneously on that event, proving the probability statement.",
    "justification": "Coverage of an optimizer set does not by itself certify the actual policy sent to deployment.",
    "gap": "ClopperPearson1934Binomial supplies cellwise coverage, but the decision-level robust regret certificate and solver-error accounting are absent from categorical-instrument policy learning.",
    "consumer": "A clinical or public-policy deployment can report an auditable upper bound on worst-case welfare loss for the mixture actually used.",
